WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
Condemned to be free.

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.330
That was how Jean-Paul Sartre
described every human being.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.420
With no God to design
human nature, he said,

4
00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:14.050
we exist first and then make
ourselves by our choices.

5
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.260
A century earlier, the Danish thinker
Søren Kierkegaard also valued freedom.

6
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.020
But for him it led to a
passionate leap of faith.

7
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:28.310
So if there is no God, are we
more free, or just more alone?

8
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.680
In this mission, you'll compare believers
and atheists who all put freedom first.

9
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.850
Then you'll weigh the charge
that religion is an escape,

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.670
and humanist ideas inside
and outside religion.

11
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.040
Your mission: weigh up whether life
without God makes us more free,

12
00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.450
or just more alone.
